se while i love how the  show's getting some love moving past the  ending sequence i legitimately enjoyed  this supernatural foray into hell  salem's lot with the ever trusty  leonardo watch on our side the episodic  nature of most of the episodes may not  be a lot for people but for those who  just wanted their dose of urban fantasy  action you'll be in for hell of a treat  studio bones really went all out for  this decently niche title to produce  what i believe is one of the best  animated action series in 2015. the  great art and animation helps support  the character writing which many  appraised and what you get is a title  that unexpectedly exceeded all  expectations that i had it's also got  another season which likewise delivered  the same goodness so the fun doesn't end  in just 12 episodes  we proceed to movieland with garden of  sinners at 6.  ah one of the many lesser-known nasu  titles garden of sinners is mostly known  for its very intricate storytelling the  mysterious aura that it carries and to a  lesser extent the breathtaking visuals  perhaps it's because people expect great  visuals from a theatrical production but  the garden of sinners movies go beyond  those expectations and shatter them over  the course of seven movies the mid to  late 2000s is still quite early in their  history but ufo table already started  showing glimpses of the future with how  the garden of sinners movie was animated  very fluid and well choreographed action  sequences get coupled with those  melancholic backdrops and detailed  environments create the mysterious air  the movie series has most of the time  the character designs are also a thing  of beauty and looking at garden of  sinners overall i guess it's a prelude  of things to come for ufo table  now before we continue i'd like to  mention that we finally have a discord  server so check the link in the  description after you finish the video  and join the community for giveaways  events anime discussion and other fun  stuff now let's continue with the video  at number five we take a look at the  newest kid on the block jujutsu kaizen  it's finally time to talk about the cool  kid of the 2020s jiu jitsu kaizen to say  the jiu jitsu kaizen's best point is the  animation i feel would be doing the  anime a very minor disservice when it  comes to the world of battle shonen i  personally feel that jiu jitsu kaizen is  more than the sparks and flashes it's  got some creative usage of its cast goes  slightly past norms while keeping in  line with the established tropes of the  genre and introduces us to some really  nice fight setups but i can't blame you  if the first thing that strikes out to  you for jiu jitsu kaizen is its  animation i mean sakuraga is just  everywhere injured to kaizen we can talk  about the hanami fight or half the  things gojo does or fushiguro's glorious  moment at the tail end of the series  almost every episode there's something  in the visual spectacle that is  jiu-jitsu kaizen that makes people's  jaws drop jiu-jitsu kaizen is the newest  addition to the ever-growing library of  anime titans to take the world by storm  and made the best entrance that anyone  could hope for  right after jiu jitsu kaizen is demon  slayer  to no one's surprise demon slayer is on  this list and yes i intentionally placed  it next to jiu jitsu kaizen because in a  more meta sense the two shows feel like  successes to each other given their  similar trajectories and success  settings changed characters change but  the whole premise of a team of  specialists fighting supernatural and  demonic beings lives on for demon slayer  everyone can talk about rui but have you  seen what ufo table did with the movie  how about the time zinitsu showed off  how badass he can be heck even in the  currently airing red light district arc  there's no shortage of demon slayer just  being  visually stunning vivid backgrounds a  bright art style that captures the vigor  of the era and spectacular